<section class="page-hero"><div class="container page-hero-grid"><div class="page-hero-card"><div class="breadcrumbs"><a href="/">Home</a> / Biography</div><p class="eyebrow">Regimental History</p><h1>The story of the Brave Rifles.</h1><p>The 3rd Cavalry Regiment traces its lineage to 1846 as the Regiment of Mounted Riflemen and later evolved through cavalry, mechanized, armored, and Stryker eras.[web:61]</p></div><div class="page-hero-art"><img src="/public/assets/hero-soldier.jpg" alt="3rd Cavalry Regiment soldier image" width="1920" height="1080" loading="lazy"></div></div></section>
<section class="section surface"><div class="container timeline"><article class="timeline-card"><h3>1846</h3><p>The regiment was constituted as the Regiment of Mounted Riflemen at Jefferson Barracks, Missouri.[web:61]</p></article><article class="timeline-card"><h3>1861</h3><p>It became the 3rd U.S. Cavalry Regiment during the Civil War era as the Army standardized cavalry units.[web:61]</p></article><article class="timeline-card"><h3>1943</h3><p>The unit shifted into the mechanized era as the 3rd Cavalry Group (Mechanized).[web:61]</p></article><article class="timeline-card"><h3>2011</h3><p>The regiment completed its conversion to the modern Stryker-based 3rd Cavalry Regiment.[web:61]</p></article></div></section>
